        "original_id": "99c542ce-28e5-55dc-a06b-4a547fe59a63",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Shenandoah Valley Regional Airport, Louisville International Airport, Staunton, Augusta County, Virginia, Louisville, Jefferson County, Kentucky, Grottoes\n- Companies: Henson Airlines, UPS Airlines\n- Systems: IATA, ICAO, FAA LID, Worldport\n- Topics: airport use, commercial airline service, air hub, aircraft accident\n\nFacts:\n- On September 23, 1985, Henson Airlines Flight 1517 crashed in Grottoes, Virginia, while approaching Shenandoah Valley Regional Airport.\n- Shenandoah Valley Regional Airport has the identifiers IATA SHD, ICAO KSHD, and FAA LID SHD.\n- Shenandoah Valley Regional Airport is a public airport located 10 nautical miles northeast of the central business district of Staunton in Augusta County, Virginia, United States.\n- Shenandoah Valley Regional Airport is used mostly for general aviation and is also served by one commercial airline.\n- Louisville International Airport has the identifiers IATA SDF, ICAO KSDF, and FAA LID SDF.\n- Louisville International Airport is a public and military-use public airport located centrally in Louisville in Jefferson County, Kentucky, United States.\n- UPS Airlines bases its international all-points air hub, Worldport, at Louisville International Airport.",
